  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1236 PM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nWednesday will feature a cold start with temps in the mid 20s to \nupper 30s. The afternoon will remain chilly, but not as cold as \nTuesday as sunshine returns. Afternoon highs should warm into the \n50s again Wednesday, but winds will remain on the breezy side \nthrough early evening before high pressure settles in and the \npressure gradient relaxes. Yet another freeze is expected Wednesday \nnight/Thursday morning, and it may impact areas along the I-35 \nCorridor and potentially locations in the Coastal Plains. We will \nhold off on any sort of freeze products for now to see how Tuesday \nnight/Wednesday morning pans out.\n\nThanksgiving day looks cold to start, but temperatures should \nrebound back into the upper 50s to lower 60s. Friday and beyond will \nbe dry as zonal flow continues with little change through the final \ndays of November. Expect temperatures to steadily climb each day, \nwith highs back in the 60s and 70s by the weekend.",
